1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,600
and by December 22, the Sun's demise was fully realized

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:07,000
for the Sun, having moved south continually for six months

3
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:10,320
makes it to its lowest point in the sky.

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,640
Here a curious thing occurs.

5
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:18,160
The Sun stops moving south, at least perceivably, for three days.

6
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:21,760
And during this three-day pause, the Sun resides in the vicinity

7
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:26,200
of the Southern Cross constellation.

8
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:31,080
And after this time, on December 25, the Sun moves one degree,

9
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:36,760
this time north, foreshadowing longer days, warmth, and spring.

10
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:41,080
And thus it was said, the Sun died on the cross,

11
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:46,520
was dead for three days, only to be resurrected or born again.

12
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:50,040
This is why Jesus and numerous other sun gods share

13
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:55,000
the crucifixion, three-day death and resurrection concept.

